From Sarah.Kraak at Marine.ie  Mon Sep 10 12:17:55 2012
From: Sarah.Kraak at Marine.ie (Sarah Kraak)
Date: Mon, 10 Sep 2012 11:17:55 +0100
Subject: [FLR-list] age and length structured simulation models using FLR
Message-ID: <80B3A3B637168240BC026CECBCE7AA663531B0D4E1@MICCRMBX.Marine.ie>

Dear FLR user,

I plan to develop a simulation model that is partly age-length-structured. For projecting the cohorts forward through time I would collapse the age-length structure to age structure, but for e.g. simulating the effect of alternative gear I would switch to length-by-age structure within the time step. Is there anybody who has experience with this? I tried to avoid reinventing the wheel if someone else already has. I haven't worked with FLR for ages (not since 2008), so at the moment I'm probably pretty ignorant. I was thinking of using the dimension "unit" within the FLQuant for the length-disaggregated data. Does that make sense? If this is stupid, please let me know.

Kind regards, and thanks a lot in advance,

Sarah

