Hi.

I cannot recall anybody doing it. If I understand correctly you want
both age and length dimensions. You could as you say use unit for this,
or, as we once planned for salmon, use a more complex naming convention
in the first 'quant' dimension that mixes both dimensions, e.g. 1_50,
1_55, 1_60, 2_50, ... Anyway, the main issue is that most methods work
on ages, so you would have to check at every step and probably rewrite
some code, or at least write some to neatly collapse by age or length

Best regards,


Iago

